Z||000000||fropuff||03-02-2001||04:07 PM||||Hey, I am thinking of selling my '86 GT.  I've driven my 1980 Oldsmobile Cutlass since I got my license, and have come to the conclusion that my Cutlass isn't going to last until summer.  I wish I could keep my GT, but I want to get a year-round car.  Here's the details:<BR>1986 Pontiac Fiero<BR>red w/ silver GFX and gray interior<BR>new paint<BR>excellent body condition<BR>PERFECT seats<BR>perfect plastic interior parts<BR>no carpet stains or tears<BR>about 63K miles<BR>transmission doesn't slip<BR>engine runs great<BR>automatic transmission<BR>everything is spotless<BR>no rust on frame, etc.<BR> <BR>The only thing it really needs is tires, a windshield, and the overheating problem needs to be fixed.  I, with the help of others, have figured that it is not caused by large things, but smaller things; thermostat, radiator clog, stat cap, radiator cap, etc.  <P>I am wondering if I would be able to get $4000 out of this, as my brother is willing to pay that (to drive it year-round  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  )  Should I be asking more or less?  Thanks a lot.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>||||reg||9
